# UICP – Deterministic Constraint Enforcement Layer for AI

## What this package contains

Public wrappers, verification scripts, external adversarial validation documents,
and the REST API gateway for the UICP constraint integrity pipeline.

## Quick Start — REST API Gateway

### 1. Build Docker Image
```bash
docker build -t uicp-gateway:latest .
```

2. Prepare Constraint Set

Save your constraint set JSON to constraint_set.json:

```json
{
  "objective_id": "LOAN_APPROVAL_V1",
  "constraints": ["age >= 18", "risk <= 25"]
}
```

3. Run Container

```bash
docker run \
  -e API_KEY="sk-test-your-api-key-here" \
  -e CONSTRAINT_SET_PATH="/etc/constraint_set.json" \
  -v $(pwd)/constraint_set.json:/etc/constraint_set.json \
  -p 5000:5000 \
  uicp-gateway:latest
```

4. Test the Gateway

```bash
curl -X POST http://localhost:5000/enforce \
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -H "X-API-Key: sk-test-your-api-key-here" \
  -d '{
    "model_output": "Loan for client age: 35. Risk score: 8. APPROVE.",
    "binding_schema": {
      "age": {"method": "regex", "pattern": "age[=: ]*(?P<value>\\d+)"},
      "risk": {"method": "regex", "pattern": "risk[=: ]*(?P<value>\\d+)"}
    },
    "constraint_set": {"objective_id": "LOAN_APPROVAL_V1", "constraints": ["age >= 18", "risk <= 25"]}
  }'
```

Endpoints

POST /enforce

Main enforcement endpoint. Accepts two modes:

Mode 1: Raw Model Output

```bash
curl -X POST http://localhost:5000/enforce \
  -H "X-API-Key: sk-test-your-key" \
  -d '{
    "model_output": "string from your model",
    "binding_schema": {variables and patterns},
    "constraint_set": {constraints to enforce}
  }'
```

Mode 2: Pre-Extracted Bindings

```bash
curl -X POST http://localhost:5000/enforce \
  -H "X-API-Key: sk-test-your-key" \
  -d '{
    "bindings": {"age": 35, "risk": 8},
    "constraint_set": {constraints to enforce}
  }'
```

GET /health

Health check endpoint.

```bash
curl http://localhost:5000/health
```

Response: {"status": "healthy"}

Environment Variables

Variable Required Description
API_KEY Yes Authentication key. Set to a strong value.
CONSTRAINT_SET_PATH Yes Path to constraint set JSON file inside container.
PERSONAL_DATA_STORE_KEY No 64-char hex encryption key for personal data (32 bytes).
PORT No Port to listen on. Default: 5000.

Response Format

Success (200)

```json
{
  "status": "ALLOW",
  "violations": [],
  "decision_id": "abc123...",
  "output_id": "APP-2024-001",
  "timestamp": "2026-05-29T12:34:56Z"
}
```

Violation (200)

```json
{
  "status": "BLOCK",
  "violations": [
    {
      "constraint_identity": "C_AGE",
      "canonical_form": "age >= 18",
      "actual_value_hash": "sha256...",
      "expected": "age >= 18"
    }
  ],
  "decision_id": "def456...",
  "output_id": "APP-2024-001",
  "timestamp": "2026-05-29T12:34:56Z"
}
```

Error (4xx/5xx)

```json
{
  "error": true,
  "error_type": "MISSING_CONSTRAINT_SET",
  "message": "constraint_set is required",
  "retryable": false,
  "request_id": "req-uuid"
}
```

Logging

All requests are logged to stdout as JSON lines. Captured by Docker logs:

```bash
docker logs <container_id>
```

Updating Constraint Set

To update the constraint set, restart the container with a new file:

```bash
vim constraint_set.json
docker restart <container_id>
```

Production Deployment

For Kubernetes:

```yaml
apiVersion: v1
kind: Pod
metadata:
  name: uicp-gateway
spec:
  containers:
  - name: gateway
    image: uicp-gateway:latest
    ports:
    - containerPort: 5000
    env:
    - name: API_KEY
      valueFrom:
        secretKeyRef:
          name: uicp-secrets
          key: api-key
    - name: CONSTRAINT_SET_PATH
      value: /etc/constraint_set.json
    volumeMounts:
    - name: constraint-set
      mountPath: /etc
    livenessProbe:
      httpGet:
        path: /health
        port: 5000
      initialDelaySeconds: 5
      periodSeconds: 10
  volumes:
  - name: constraint-set
    configMap:
      name: constraint-set-config
```

